lambdock (0.23.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New upstream release. Breaking: every theme and look is named after its
    material instead of the desktop it was traced from, and the old names and
    short aliases are removed. macos-tiger/osx-tiger is brushed,
    snow-leopard/osx-snow-leopard is frost (dark: frost-dark),
    macos-mavericks/osx-mavericks is platinum (dark: platinum-dark),
    macos-big-sur/osx-big-sur is dune, macos-ventura/osx-ventura is stage,
    macos-tahoe/osx-tahoe is glass (dark: glass-dark), windows-xp is luna,
    windows-vista is aurora, windows-7 is seven, windows-10 is tiles,
    windows-11 is island and unity is ambiance.
  * Popover menus keep the dock's material: the shelf modifier no longer
    repaints them, and every hovered row clears WCAG AA contrast.
  * The shelf is laid out on the first frame rather than on the next reload.

 -- Josep Bigorra <jjbigorra@gmail.com>  Thu, 05 Nov 2026 09:00:00 +0100

lambdock (0.22.2-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New upstream release: one fix. Every running application painted two
    indicators -- the theme's dot at the bottom of its button and the glass
    shelf's bead on the slab -- because the rule meant to silence the theme's dot
    was in shelf.css, which is loaded before the theme: GTK resolves competing
    declarations from providers of the same priority by the order they were
    added, not by selector specificity, so the rule always lost. It is now a
    guard provider attached after the theme, only while the glass actually draws
    the bead.

 -- Josep Bigorra <jjbigorra@gmail.com>  Mon, 02 Nov 2026 08:40:00 +0100

lambdock (0.22.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New upstream release: three fixes to what the dock draws and what it reads.
    Separators, gauges and clocks reserve the reflection band but have no
    artwork, so they no longer paint the icon's contact shadow under a line; the
    running indicator is a crisp bar again, larger than the reference's
    proportions and over a pool tight enough to be seen against; and local state
    is picked up as it is written, because the dock now watches
    ~/.local/state/lambdock (where the Preferences overrides and the
    drag-and-drop layout live) and persists a preference before applying it
    rather than after.

 -- Josep Bigorra <jjbigorra@gmail.com>  Mon, 02 Nov 2026 08:10:00 +0100

lambdock (0.22.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New upstream release: the Platinum material is read off the reference dock's own
    artwork, and an icon dragged out of the dock leaves in a puff of smoke. The
    install media carries the reference dock, so the platinum slab's lip, its
    drop shadow, the running indicator, the folder panel and the separator are
    the images' own values: a 1px black lip with 2px of white in front of it,
    that white brightening from 0.56 at the dock's ends to 0.82 in the middle;
    black at 0.60 against the slab fading over 18px; a white bead on a cyan
    glow; charcoal rgb(33,33,33) at 0.85 with a rgb(200,200,200) bevel for stack
    panels; and a two-pixel engraved divider. The side-dock indicator is its own
    image rather than the bottom one rotated, the icon's contact shadow is an
    elliptical Gaussian pool again instead of a linear band, and the menus use
    the reference dock's wording ("Open", "View content as"). Dragging an icon out of the
    dock plays the five-frame poof the real dock had, and the layout closes the
    gap once the smoke clears.

 -- Josep Bigorra <jjbigorra@gmail.com>  Mon, 02 Nov 2026 07:40:00 +0100

lambdock (0.21.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New upstream release: the round that finished the refactor list, with no
    behaviour change. The meter's geometry and colour thresholds are pure, tested
    values; the shelf's value types moved to core/shelf_params.h so the pure core
    headers no longer include the application or a widget header; the
    desktop-entry cache is one value; the icon search paths are built from
    explicit inputs; main.c and the preferences window use the registry visitor
    instead of hand-rolled snapshot loops; and the window model (tracking,
    running/focused/minimized styling, app-id lookup) moved out of dock_item.c
    into dock_item_windows.c. Dynamic-item pollers now go through the Guile
    bridge, so no scm_* call lives outside guile_bridge.c and lambdock.h no
    longer includes libguile.h.

 -- Josep Bigorra <jjbigorra@gmail.com>  Sat, 31 Oct 2026 18:00:00 +0100

lambdock (0.20.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New upstream release: two theme families and the dock's first whole-dock
    recipes. Brushed and Glass (light and dark) join Frost, Platinum,
    Dune and Stage, which now carry their own 3D shelf material, and the
    Aurora and Seven join Luna, Tiles and Island; the five
    taskbar looks are one family -- all taskbars, all 32px icons, all flat -- and
    differ only where their era did. Twenty look recipes set the theme, the sizes,
    the shelf geometry, the window titles and the fisheye in one line
    (`(define dock-look 'platinum-dark)`), with aliases and an
    `(apply-look!)` for the REPL. Every theme was audited state by state (focused
    window, labels, light-slab indicators), and theme scoping no longer loses a
    selector written across two lines. The launchpad loses its title and puts its
    close button on the left by default (a setting moves it right), and the
    Preferences window gains a "Dock items" card that adds a trash can, a clock or
    a RAM/CPU/temperature/battery meter to the dock.

 -- Josep Bigorra <jjbigorra@gmail.com>  Sat, 31 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0100

lambdock (0.15.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New upstream release: the project is licensed under the MIT License instead
    of the GPL-3.0-or-later, and every file carries the SPDX header and the
    copyright line. Stacks drop the fan view: the icon grid and the list remain,
    and a settings file or layout override that still says 'fan reads back as the
    grid, so nothing breaks. The C side was reworked around explicit models --
    the launchpad, the preferences window and the active-dock registry -- with
    the search filter, the column arithmetic and the configuration limits moved
    into pure, tested functions. Nothing else changes for users.

 -- Josep Bigorra <jjbigorra@gmail.com>  Wed, 28 Oct 2026 10:00:00 +0100

lambdock (0.13.3-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New upstream release: the launchpad lists one tile per application again,
    collapsing the desktop files that describe the same program, and a tile
    whose application is installed more than once offers every copy from its
    context menu with where each copy comes from and the command it runs. The
    launchpad backdrop is denser, so its labels read over a busy desktop.

 -- Josep Bigorra <jjbigorra@gmail.com>  Tue, 27 Oct 2026 15:05:00 +0100

lambdock (0.13.2-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New upstream release: the right-click menu of a dock item carries actions
    that fit the application. Browsers get New Window and New Private Window
    with the flag their family expects, and a running music player gets
    Play/Pause, Previous, Next and Stop over MPRIS. The kind is read from the
    desktop entry's Categories=, falling back to the id, name and command line.

 -- Josep Bigorra <jjbigorra@gmail.com>  Mon, 26 Oct 2026 20:30:00 +0100

